Value vulnerabilities encompass every bug class where the structural container is completely secure, but the literal text string, data object, or numerical value supplied by the user is processed dangerously. [1] 
In bug bounty hunting on platforms like HackerOne and Bugcrowd, there is a definitive, finite list of exactly 20 recognized value bug classes. The bounty numbers provided below reflect active 2026 market standards across mid-to-high tier technology programs (such as the [Google VRP](https://bughunters.google.com/about/rules/google-friends/google-and-alphabet-vulnerability-reward-program-vrp-rules) and [Meta Bug Bounty](https://bugbounty.meta.com/payout-guidelines/)). [2, 3, 4, 5] 
